/-! # The Seventh source vector with literal octad blocks

The octad blocks of `seventhSrcVecL` (the `Ko`-scaled octad Fourier transforms `twTriOct` of the
merged blocks of the word image) are evaluated once, in chunks, and replaced by literal blocks;
the matrix block gets an integer form for the factory matrix parts.  The resulting vector
`seventhSrcVecF` is `seventhSrcVecW 64`, so it represents family representative
`6`. -/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
namespace FormalizedTextbooks.FrenkelLepowskyMeurmanMonster
